# NET-TELEPORT-ENCROACH: a server teleport lands the pawn on a valid spot (UE AActor::TeleportTo ->
# UWorld::FindTeleportSpot; AGameModeBase::RestartPlayer through the same placement). The simulation holds a pending
# placement per pawn (Net/MeshOfOne.hpp Pawn::Pending), asks the server's world whether the destination is resident
# (Net::IWorldResidency, ServerWorld::ResidencyAt) and the game where the capsule may stand (Net::IPawnPlacer,
# Gameplay::FindTeleportSpot: lifted out of the ground, snapped onto the floor, refused over nothing). A falling
# pawn never passes 4000 cm/s (Gameplay::kTerminalVelocityCmPerS).
# Before this feature (scn-1127-020957): `teleport 1 40000 300 3000` put the capsule 276 cm under the landscape
# (ground 576 cm) and the pawn fell for 116 s to y=-6.66e6 (server.log:1246); a teleport to (200000, 300, 3000), in
# no cell of the grid, was accepted. The console printed nothing but "player N has no pawn".
# Played by scripts/Dev/net_scenario.py. A's frames come from its pawn camera (--shot-player-view): the landing is what
# A sees. A sprints +X; its scripted walk ends at 300 m (server position), and the teleports come after it stopped, so
# no input moves the landed pawn and the residency union 5 s later must hold the very spot. B joins only then, so
# every pawn-1 velocity B ever receives is after the walk (a non-zero one is the slide of D4).
# Net coordinates are Y-up (X, Y, Z), cm.
Мир Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
Роль server server --role all --source 0,0,0 --pawn assets:Prefabs/Pawn_Player.deprefab --spawn 0,-300,1150 --spawn 500,-300,-200 --steps 864000
Ждать server 60 \[Server\] listening on port
Роль A editor account=1 lag=75 loss=2 --play --shot-frames 100000 --shot-every 1 --shot-player-view --quality PostProcess.MotionBlurQuality=0 --net-walk-cm 30000 --net-walk-dir 1,0,0 --net-walk-mode sprint
Ждать A 1800 \[Net\] in session
# 1. The spawn goes through the placer: the pawn lands on the floor under (0, -300, 1150) (the floor is at -382 there,
# scn-1127-020957/server.log:82) and the server's line names how it was found.
Ждать server 60 player 1 \(account 1\): pawn net id 1 spawned
Ждать server 60 player 1: pawn 1 spawned onto \(0, -3[0-9]\d, 1150\) cm: .*(free|lifted|snapped)
# The scripted sprint ends (300 m of server position).
Ждать A 900 \[Net\] walked \d+ cm \(server position\): stopping
Роль B bot account=2 lag=75 loss=2 --seconds 1500
Ждать server 120 player 2 \(account 2\): pawn net id \d+ spawned
# 2. Teleport into the ground: (40000, 300, 3000) is 276 cm under the landscape (576 cm). The capsule is lifted onto
# the surface (feet = ground + 2 cm skin), Grounded, velocity zero.
Консоль server teleport 1 40000 300 3000
Ждать server 120 player 1: pawn 1 teleported to \(40000, 5[6-9]\d, 3000\) cm: .*lifted 2\d\d cm
# The own client takes the position AND the zero velocity (NET-TELEPORT-VELOCITY).
Ждать A 120 correction \d+ at input step \d+: the server has the own pawn at \(40000\.0, 5[6-9]\d\.\d, 3000\.0\) cm.*server v \(0, 0, 0\)
Тогда A tp_ground the frame of that correction tick from A's pawn camera: the landscape surface under the camera and the horizon in front - not the terrain's underside, not a void; the view is at standing height
